      "note": "No limit is drawn for this model, and the reason is structural rather than a missing setting. It reports five observables -- three species plus total_biomass and n_survivors -- against a three-component ODE, and the bridge overlays the limit column by column and in order, so it refuses anything that does not correspond one-to-one. Any model reporting DERIVED observables alongside its state has the same problem. The refusal is correct: silently drawing the ODE's three columns against the first three observables would happen to be right here and would be wrong for a model that ordered them differently."
